jq("j-f-stream-sorted", "Streams: sorted with a Lambda", "MEDIUM", T, "Read `n` students (`name marks`). Use `sorted` with a lambda comparator to print them by marks from highest to lowest (equal marks by name), one `name marks` per line.", "First line `n`, then `n` lines `name marks`.", "`n` lines.", "1 <= n <= 50",
   'List<String[]> rows = new ArrayList<>();\nfor (int i = 0; i < n; i++) rows.add(new String[] {in.next(), in.next()});\nrows.stream().sorted((x, y) -> {\n    int c = Integer.compare(Integer.parseInt(y[1]), Integer.parseInt(x[1]));\n    return c != 0 ? c : x[0].compareTo(y[0]);\n}).forEach(r -> System.out.println(r[0] + " " + r[1]));', ["3\nasha 82\nravi 91\nmeena 77", "1\nk 50", "4\nzed 50\namy 50\nbob 70\ncat 50", "2\nb 1\na 1", "3\nx 9\ny 9\nz 10"], JN, imports=ST)
